208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Our findings show that audience discourse plays a big role in shaping the perception between Angel Reese and Caitlan Clark. Platform differences can amplify rivalry narratives, as demonstrated especially on YouTube, with higher cross-reference rates and more competitive and dismissive framing. This suggests that social media audiences and third party media sources actively contribute to constructing and reinforcing the rivalry perception. Understanding how these narratives develop can help sport organizations, media professionals, and athletes better manage public perception and support the growth of womens sports. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
